# JUCE 8 WebView

Factory CMake sets `JUCE_WEB_BROWSER=0`. Do not add a WebView unless the product's design spec turns that flag on and the target is JUCE 8.

When it is on, bind parameters with the JUCE 8 relays. Do not invent a JUCE 6/7 `LookAndFeel` for that UI.

```cpp
juce::WebSliderRelay cutoffRelay { "cutoff" };
juce::WebBrowserComponent web {
    juce::WebBrowserComponent::Options{}
        .withOptionsFrom(cutoffRelay)
};
// member lives as long as the relay
juce::WebSliderParameterAttachment cutoffAttachment {
    *apvts.getParameter("cutoff"), cutoffRelay };
```

JavaScript uses `Juce.getSliderState("cutoff")` from `juce-framework-frontend`. The same pattern exists for `WebToggleButtonRelay` and `WebComboBoxRelay`. Read `juce_WebControlRelays.h` for the target JUCE before writing a new call. Fetch JUCE docs with Context7 when the header is not in the tree.
